---
title: "Active Overlay"
---

Applications can display an overlay on demand regardless of grid state. This is achieved by providing an active overlay which can be one of the provided overlays or be a custom overlay component.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Active Overlay (Component Class)" name="active-overlay-component" exampleHeight=350 /%}

## Display an Active Overlay

To display an overlay on demand set the `activeOverlay` / `activeOverlayParams` grid option. To clear the overlay set `activeOverlay = undefined`.

{% apiDocumentation source="grid-options/properties.json" section="overlays" names=["activeOverlay", "activeOverlayParams"] /%}

## Status Announcements

Provided overlays shown with `activeOverlay` announce through their own `role="status"` message element; `activeOverlay: 'agLoadingOverlay'` uses the loading overlay's own status element for loading and completion announcements.

A custom active overlay is application-owned. AG Grid mounts the component but does not infer status announcements from its DOM text, because the component can contain arbitrary content. If the overlay represents a status, progress, or blocking state that should be announced, include a live region in the custom overlay component, such as a visually hidden element with `role="status"`, `aria-live="polite"` and `aria-atomic="true"`.

The custom overlay example on this page includes a hidden status element that is updated from the same params as the visible overlay content.

{% if isFramework("javascript", "angular") %}
Implement the `IOverlayComp` interface to provide a custom overlay the grid will supply `IOverlayParams` whenever the component is created or refreshed.
{% /if %}
{% if isFramework("angular") %}
